        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "87c86069-563a-58a5-9cce-b4831222f3a6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: The Tarnished Eye\n- People: Judith Guest, John Norman Collins\n- Events: Robison family murders, Michigan Murders\n- Places: Good Hart, Ann Arbor, Ypsilanti, Michigan\n\nFacts:\n- The Robison family murders occurred in June 1968 in Good Hart, Michigan.\n- Between 1967 and 1969, the Michigan Murders were a highly publicized series of killings of young women in the Ann Arbor and Ypsilanti area of Southeastern Michigan.\n- The killer in the Michigan Murders was known as the Ypsilanti Ripper, the Michigan Murderer, and the Co-Ed Killer.\n- In the late 1960s, John Norman Collins committed murders in the Ann Arbor and Ypsilanti areas of Michigan.\n- The Tarnished Eye is a 2004 crime novel by Judith Guest.\n- The Tarnished Eye is based on the Robison family murders and on murders committed by John Norman Collins.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
